# Project One Get-Item Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: get-item and inventory design for M7 Project Two
#
# Review the course-provided get-item flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, SET, ADD, or similar terms.

START get_item

SET current_room
SET item_in_room
SET inventory

PROMPT player to enter "get" followed by the item they want
 GET player_command

IF requested item is in current_room
        ADD requested item to inventory
        REMOVE requested item from current_room
        DISPLAY "You picked up the " + requested item 
 ELSE 
     DISPLAY "You cannot get that item because it is not here."

RETURN to the main game loop 
PROMPT player for next command

END get_item


